  "preamble": "Deglottalization of the postalveolar ejective affricate [t͡ʃʼ] to plain [t͡ʃ]. Spanish has no ejectives and renders Quechua ch' [t͡ʃʼ] as ch [t͡ʃ]. The evidence is weak in two ways. Within Southern Quechua, Ayacucho Quechua and Santiagueño lack the ejective series that Cusco–Collao has (Wikipedia, Southern Quechua). So the Spanish words may come from forms that never had an ejective. Spanish chullo is left out because its donor ch'ullu also has the form chullu.",
